Add the <cstdint> includes GCC 13 and later require.

RocksDB 7.9 relies on transitive <cstdint> includes that libstdc++ 13 removed,
so uint16_t/uint32_t are undeclared in these headers and the build fails.

Origin: upstream, https://github.com/facebook/rocksdb/pull/11118
Description: include <cstdint> in the two headers that use fixed-width ints
Forwarded: not-needed, fixed upstream in RocksDB 8.0
--- a/table/block_based/data_block_hash_index.h
+++ b/table/block_based/data_block_hash_index.h
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <string>
 #include <vector>
 
--- a/util/string_util.h
+++ b/util/string_util.h
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 #pragma once
 
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <sstream>
 #include <string>
 #include <unordered_map>
